EXT. WHALE-RIB BRIDGE - DUSK

A bridge of bleached ribs over a gorge. Fog below. A toll hut perched at the midpoint.

GRUB MAWDLEY, goblin, one eye, sits on the toll barrel. Chewing.

Two pilgrims approach: TAMSIN, young, sword too big for her, and ROOK, old, hooded, leaning on a staff.

Behind them, a STRANGER in grey rags, bare feet. Silent. Following.

MAWDLEY
Toll. Two coppers. Each.

TAMSIN
(to Rook)
He's got no right. The queen abolished tolls.

ROOK
(muttering)
Queens abolish. Goblins collect.

MAWDLEY
Three coppers. I heard that.

TAMSIN
Fine.

She counts coins. Mawdley bites each one. The Stranger steps up beside them.

MAWDLEY (CONT'D)
And you? Rags. Nothing to pay with?

STRANGER
I pay differently.

MAWDLEY
Everybody says that.

TAMSIN
Don't test him.

MAWDLEY ^
Don't test me.

Tamsin and Mawdley glare at each other. Fog thickens. The ribs begin to hum.

ROOK
(to everyone)
Step back. All of you. Now.

The Stranger throws back the hood. Silver hair. Eyes like struck flint.

STRANGER
Zephyrine.

Mawdley drops the coin. The bridge SHUDDERS.

ZEPHYRINE
I built this bridge. You've been charging for my bones.

MAWDLEY
(whispering)
Oh, no.

The ribs CRACK. Light floods upward from the gorge.
